<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<model version="NetLogo 7.0.0" snapToGrid="false">
  <code><![CDATA[; Creating turtle variable
turtles-own [ money]

; Creating the setup procedure
; In setup procedure we usually define all the model initial conditions

to setup
  ca ; Each time that we run this procedure the model will be reset.

  ; Create the turtles and define the values for the variables
  ; Since in this model the spatial location of turtles is not relevant, we
  ;create all the turtles in the same patch.
  create-turtles 100 [ set money 100 ]

  ; Since we are going to take into account the timing in which actions are carried out
  ;in the model, each time we set up our model, we have to reset the time by using the
  ;primitive reset-ticks

  ; "reset-ticks" - >  Resets the tick counter to zero, sets up all plots, then updates all plots

  reset-ticks
end

to go
 ; Since we do not want to run the model forever, we must specify a stop condition
 ; In order to do that, we will use the "ticks" and "stop" primitives
 ; "ticks" -> report the current value of the tick
 ; "stop" -> stop the "go" procedure.
 if (ticks = 50000) [stop]

 ; We order to a subset of turtles (those with money greater than zero according to
;our model specification)...

  ask turtles with [ money > 0 ]
  ; ... to give money to other turtles...
  [ give_money ]

  ; After agent(s) have performed the actions, we use "tick" to count by one the time and update plots
  tick
end

; Note 1: 'go' procedure has this structure:

; to procedure_A
;    procedure_B
; end


; Note 2: Do not forget to mark the check box 'forever' when you create the GO button.
;Thus, you will not have to press the button each time that you run a simulation.

to give_money
  ; First, the chosen turtle is going to randomly choose another
  ask one-of other turtles

  ; If you do not specify "other turtles", the turtle which is selecting could select
  ;herself. Which it is not necessarily an error but it would be an incorrect
  ;specification given our model description.

  ; Then the turtle asks the 'other' turtle to increase its money by one.
  [ set money money + 1]
  ; and, finally, the requester turtle lose one euro
  set money money - 1
end


;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

; Creting a plot: Histogram

;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

; So far, when we run this simulation it looks like if nothing is happening, which is false.
; In order to observe the model behavior over time, we are going to create a histogram.

; Steps:

; (1) Go to interface tab
; (2) Press right-click on any white place
; (3) Select plot
; (4) In plot setup commands use the following code to select the number of bars
;in the histogram (in this case we have defined 40 bars):
; set-histogram-num-bars 40
; (5) In plot pens, you can define:
; - Color: the color of the bars
; - Pen name: A personalized name for the legend
; - Pen update commands: whatever you want to plot.
;In this case, we select the money of the turtles using the following code:
; histogram [money] of turtles

; Finally, press the pencil icon and select in 'advanced pen option' the alternative 'bar'.
; Now you run again the simulation (Press SETUP and then GO) and you will observe how the money distribution looks over time.

; Uncheck 'autoscale'
; x = 0 - 400
; y = 0 - 15


;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

; Creting monitors

;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

; Another way of observing the model behavior is through monitors. In this particular case,
;we can monitor both the proportion of money in the system owned by the 15% richer and
;by the 15% poorer.

; "max-n-of" -> Reports an agentset containing number agents from agentset with the highest values of reporter.
; Structure -> max-n-of + number + agentset + [reporter or variable]

; We can create the following monitors:

; (a) The proportion of total money by the richest 15%:

; sum [money] of max-n-of 15 turtles [ money]    /     sum [money] of turtles

; (b) The proportion of total money by the poorest 15%:

; sum [money] of min-n-of 15 turtles [ money]    /     sum [money] of turtles


; Alternatively, we can print the money of the richest turtles in the system by:
;print [money] of max-n-of 15 turtles [  money]

;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

; Practical exercises to be done during the class

;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

; (*) In another NetLogo file, extend the previous model by...

; (a) Creating a new procedure to specify:
; Turtles die when running out of money (Go to the NetLogo library and look at the primitive ‘die’)

; (b) Create a monitor to observe how many turtles there are in the world

; (c) Make 50% of the turtles turn red and 50% turn green and set up the next statement:
; agents only can give money to agents of the color red.


;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

; Exporting results

;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

; (1) Creating an output window in the interface.

; We can add the the "go" procedure the following code:
; output-print [money] of turtles
; Then, we can copy the output we get and paste it in other software.

; (2) Using the primitive: "export-world"

; If you just need the final result, you can add to the "go" procedure:
; export-world "test.csv"
; You will get a file with all the current characteristics of the world (patches,
;turtles, links,etc.).
; The file is saved in the same folder where the model is located.

; If the name of the file is not changed in the "go" procedure, the new information will
;be overwritten in the old file.

; (3) Using "Behaviorspace" (next model)]]></code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="2" wrappingAllowedX="true" y="8" frameRate="30.0" minPycor="-16" height="362" showTickCounter="true" patchSize="10.85" fontSize="10" wrappingAllowedY="true" width="362" tickCounterLabel="ticks" maxPycor="16" updateMode="0" maxPxcor="16" minPxcor="-16"></view>
    <button x="479" y="31" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="63">setup</button>
    <button x="467" y="168" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="true" kind="Observer" width="63">go</button>
    <plot x="397" autoPlotX="false" yMax="15.0" autoPlotY="false" y="395" xMin="0.0" height="196" legend="false" xMax="400.0" yMin="0.0" width="334" display="plot 1">
      <setup>set-histogram-num-bars 40</setup>
      <update></update>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="1" display="default" color="-16777216" legend="true">
        <setup></setup>
        <update>histogram [money] of turtles</update>
      </pen>
    </plot>
    <monitor x="508" precision="17" y="302" height="60" fontSize="11" width="100">count turtles</monitor>
  </widgets>
